WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.609
LSpeaker 1: et's speak next to Isaac from
Wyoming.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:08.940
Isaac from Wyoming, please.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.980
Speaker 3: Hello, David.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:12.980
Thanks for taking my call.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.860
I appreciate you taking a chance on somebody
from Wyoming.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:17.990
I love Wyoming.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.070
Thank you.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.140
Have you been to Wyoming?

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.140
Never.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.140
Speaker 1: But I would like to go.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.740
I hear that, you know, there's like a big
sky there and stuff.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.800
Speaker 3: Yeah, Big Sky and bad politics.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.340
OK.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.470
So I guess my question is it's kind of silly
because I sort of already know the answer,

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:45.980
and honestly, I just jumped in here and am
admittedly not completely prepared, but my

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:52.890
question is, do you have any plans in the
future to sort of hire your own investigative

00:00:52.890 --> 00:01:00.180
journalist, which I have seen you've been
doing somewhat recently and sort of just expand

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.860
into a legitimate news outlet?

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:08.330
Speaker 1: Well, we are completely illegitimate
currently, and so your concern is certainly

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:09.330
warranted.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.080
Will we ever have an air of legitimacy?

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.080
That's fair.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.800
Many people ask me that that that that's a
fair question.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.270
No, I know what you're saying.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.830
I mean, we're a commentary and analysis show.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.140
We're not a news reporting show, and we don't
we don't pretend otherwise.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.140
Yeah.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.140
Maybe I'm open.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.300
I'm always open to considering anything.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.600
I just think we have to think about, like
as a small organization, if we hire one investigative

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.500
reporter, what can we really do something
that we feel is meaningful and we can feel

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.480
good about compared to entities with just
overwhelmingly more resources, but I have

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.510
no opposition to it in principle.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.460
Speaker 3: Awesome.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.410
Other than that.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.370
One more question.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:58.270
As someone who's more left leaning and a red
state, what types of things would you recommend

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:05.790
for people in my situation to sort of influence
politics in the state and push it towards

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.979
the left sport
Speaker 1: in many red states where there's

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:15.020
like a tradition of voting for Republicans,
but people are actually open to different

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.300
ideas.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.850
Getting involved in ballot initiatives can
be really effective because rather than saying,

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:25.250
Hey, vote for this Democrat, which maybe isn't
going to happen, you can find ballot initiatives

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:34.020
that are reasonable moves to the left that
will not seem as scary to a Republican electorate.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.610
And so I would look at getting involved in
ballot initiatives, whether they be about

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.540
campaign finance, the environment, whatever's
important to you.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.650
Speaker 3: Awesome, yeah.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:49.190
Actually, Naomi, there there is an ongoing
effort to create a ballot initiative to legalize

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:58.460
marijuana that has thus failed so far because
the signature requirements are so big, you

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.390
know, we just can't get their signature requirements.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.730
Yes.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.150
In any case, thanks for talking to me and
I love the show.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.459
Speaker 1: All right, thank you so much.

00:03:07.459 --> 00:03:11.240
Let us know if you make any headway there
in in Wyoming

